{
  "_help": "Basic attack skills (scripts/Attacks.cs, menu: O or Skills > Basic attacks). Each weapon class has one, used by the attack button whenever that class is equipped. The player builds its chain from unlocked steps (light attacks run the chain in order, then start over) and sockets modifiers into it, like supports on spells. Unlocking steps and modifiers and ranking up costs skill points (the same points as spells). Steps: base = which of the weapon's combo swings (data/weapons.json) to borrow timing and hand poses from, 'power' for the power attack; then any of dmg (x weapon damage), arc, range, knock, stun, up, lunge, spin, critBonus, finisher, speed (x attack speed), stamina (x cost), status {id: chance}, and for ranged classes shots, spread (degrees), pierce, aoe (m). The 'start' steps are free and form the first chain.",
  "maxRank": 5,
  "rankDmgP": 8,
  "chainByRank": [3, 4, 5, 6, 7],
  "socketsByRank": [1, 1, 2, 2, 3],
  "_animHelp": "anim = the attack animation a step plays (data/avatar.json \"attackAnims\"); powerAnim = the power attack's. rec (optional, per step) = the follow-through animation during its recovery.",
